Temporary Safety and Investigation Integrity Measures
(12)
Pending investigation of a matter and having regard to the nature of the alleged conduct and potential risks, the Pro Vice-Chancellor (Student Experience and Employability) may:
approve the implementation of temporary health and safety and/or investigation integrity measures, including
changes to the student’s placement location, class, exam timetable or office location;
a direction to the student that they do not contact a member or members of the University community or discuss a matter under investigation;
any other risk mitigation measures appropriate in the circumstances that are consistent with University legislation and/or any relevant delegation.
recommend to the Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Academic) that:
they prohibit a student temporarily from attending any University campus, facility, including student accommodation, and/or University-managed or approved activity or event (e.g. a student placement, orientation event, excursion, tour or conference);
they approve conditions being placed on the student’s enrolment, for instance that they temporarily transfer to an equivalent online course.

Part B - Hearing and Determination by General Misconduct Officer
(16)
The Office of Integrity and Investigations provides support and assistance to General Misconduct Officers, who will hear and determine alleged general misconduct.
(17)
The General Misconduct Officer may:
dismiss the referral and take no further action (e.g., if the alleged conduct does not constitute general misconduct or there is insufficient evidence to support such a finding);
refer the matter to Safer Community for informal resolution;
seek further information and, in complex cases, may approve the appointment of a specialist investigator;
provide the student alleged to have committed general misconduct an opportunity to respond before making a finding as to whether general misconduct has occurred and what sanction, if any, may be appropriate in the circumstances; and/or
take any other reasonable action appropriate in all the circumstances.
